  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_041, 0.725 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer + weighted. All high-performing experiments have used imagenet_vit_l; the image encoder axis is completely unexplored in the promising regime. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200 >> scgpt), profile setting (multi >> single), and aggregation (transformer >= avgpool) effects are already well-characterized. Question: Does swapping imagenet_vit_l for resnet50 (config_015) meaningfully change performance while holding scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion constant? This isolates the image encoder effect in the high-performing region. Why this is the best next experiment: It is the single largest untested design axis in the regime where performance is already strong (~0.72). If resnet50 performs comparably, it informs cost/efficiency trade-offs; if it degrades significantly, it confirms imagenet_vit_l is a critical component and narrows future search. No other single-variable experiment in the available set would reduce as much uncertainty about a major design choice."
}

